   <!-- Exercise --> 
   <div class="watch-exercise"> 
    <div class="watch-exercise__visual" data-visible-text> 
     <div class="common__inner"> 
      <h2 class="common__headline" data-copy-set="C017-001">Find your pace, race your way</h2> 
     </div> 
     <div class="watch-exercise__image"> 
      <picture data-media-lazy> 
       <source data-empty media="(min-width:0px)" srcset="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAHAAACH5BAEAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAICRAEAOw=="> 
       <source media="(min-width: 768px)" srcset="https://images.samsung.com/pk/galaxy-watch8/feature/galaxy-watch8-exercise-lifestyle.jpg?imbypass=true"> 
       <source media="(max-width: 767px)" srcset="https://images.samsung.com/pk/galaxy-watch8/feature/galaxy-watch8-exercise-lifestyle-mo.jpg?imbypass=true"> 
       <img src="https://images.samsung.com/pk/galaxy-watch8/feature/galaxy-watch8-exercise-lifestyle.jpg?imbypass=true" alt="A woman is running outdoors wearing Galaxy Watch8." data-copy-set="C017-002"> 
      </picture> 
     </div> 
    </div> 
    <div class="watch-exercise__content"> 
     <div class="common__inner"> 
      <h3 class="common__label" data-copy-set="C018-001">Running Coach</h3> 
      <p class="common__title" data-copy-set="C018-002"> Run at your<br class="common-br-mo"> own pace with<br class="common-br-mo"> a personal coach </p> 
      <div class="watch-exercise__text"> 
       <p class="common__description" data-copy-set="C018-003"> Once you've fully recovered with a good night's sleep, it's time to move. Start with a test to identify your running level from 1 to 10. Set your goals and work your way to break them by <strong>training at your own pace</strong>. Whether you're taking your first stride as a beginner or training for a full marathon, a <strong>3-5 week running coach program tailored to your running capacity</strong> will guide and motivate you through every milestone, helping you break barriers. <sup><a href="#desc-section" class="click_sup" title="See disclaimer" data-sup="2">2</a>,<a href="#desc-section" class="click_sup" title="See disclaimer" data-sup="15">15</a></sup> </p> 
       <button type="button" class="common__video-button js-layer-opener js-howto-popup-opener" aria-label="How to use Running Coach. Open video popup" data-omni-type="microsite_contentinter" data-omni="gwatch8:highlights:exercise^running-coaching:lypu-open:how-to-use-running-coaching" ga-ca="content click" ga-ac="feature" ga-la="gwatch8:highlights:exercise^running-coaching:lypu-open:how-to-use-running-coaching" data-target-layer="#layer-popup-how-to" data-youtube-id="nh16o10JOR4" data-youtube-title="How to use Running Coach" data-howto-slide="how-to-use-running-coach" data-theme="white"> 
        <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
         <use xlink:href="#wearable-play-button" href="#wearable-play-button"></use> 
        </svg> <span class="button-text" data-copy-set="C018-006">How to use Running Coach</span> <span class="blind" aria-hidden="true" data-copy-set="C018-007"> Text in the middle: How to use Running Coach on Galaxy Watch8. New text appears: Want to become a better runner? New text appears: Run at your own pace with your watch. New text appears: Let's get started. Scene changes, text appears at the top: First, pair your watch with your phone. Galaxy Watch8 and smartphone appear from left and right. New text appears: Tap 'Connect'. Galaxy Watch8 screen displays text Welcome and smartphone screen displays a popup with Galaxy Watch8 turning 360 degrees. Text Galaxy Watch8, A new device has been detected. At the bottom are buttons Cancel and Connect. Connect button is tapped. Sequences shortened. Galaxy S25 Ultra sold separately. Video simulated for illustrative purposes. Actual UI may be different. Galaxy Watch8 Series or later must be paired with a smartphone with Android 11.0 or above and minimum 1.5 gigabyte Memory. Scene changes, text appears in the middle: To receive effective training, let's check your running level first. On the right is Galaxy Watch8. On the left, text appears: On your watch,. Galaxy Watch8 screen is swiped to the right. Running coach feature is onscreen with number 1 icon, text Running coach, Find your running level. On the left, new text appears: tap 'Find your running level'. Galaxy Watch8 screen is tapped. Find your running level is onscreen. On the left, new text appears: Scroll down, then tap 'Start survey'. Galaxy Watch8 screen is scrolled down and two buttons appear: Start survey and Settings. Start survey button is tapped. Scene changes. On the left is text Enter your profile. On the right is a smartphone with the profile creation page onscreen, the necessary information filled in. The screen is scrolled down and two buttons appear: Cancel and Save. Save button is tapped. The survey page is onscreen. On the left, new text appears: Add info on your previous running experience. Smartphone screen is scrolled down and 5 kilometer option for Distance running experience survey question is selected. Next button is tapped. Sequences shortened. Galaxy S25 Ultra sold separately. Video simulated for illustrative purposes. Actual UI may be different. Galaxy Watch8 Series or later must be paired with a smartphone with Android 11.0 or above and minimum 1.5 gigabyte Memory. Scene changes. On the right is Galaxy Watch8 with Running level test onscreen, displaying instructions. On the left, text appears: Let's start the running test! New text appears: Scroll down and read the instructions. Galaxy Watch8 screen is scrolled down. Two buttons appear: Start and Settings. On the left, new text appears: Tap 'Start' to begin. Start button on Galaxy Watch8 is tapped. Screen changes and displays the time, Duration, Distance, Pace and heart rate. On the left, new text appears: Run for 12 minutes to finish the test. Galaxy Watch8 screen displays 12 minutes, 100% of goal and confetti in the background. Screen changes and from the top text RPE with information icon, text How hard did that feel?, number 5, text Slightly hard and Done button. On the left, new text appears: Let's check 'RPE' (Rating of Perceived Exertion). Information icon on Galaxy Watch8 is tapped. About RPE is onscreen with details on what RPE is. On the left, new text appears: an index that shows the intensity of the run. Galaxy Watch8 screen is scrolled down. On the left, new text appears: on a scale of 1 to 10. The lower button on the side of Galaxy Watch8 is pressed and the screen displays RPE again. On the left, new text appears: Select the RPE of your run. On Galaxy Watch8, RPE changes from 5 to 3 and text below the number is Moderate. Done button is tapped. Number 3 icon and text Level 3 appear onscreen along with confetti in the background. On the left, new text appears: Ta-da! Here's your running level. Galaxy Watch8 displays text Your running level, number 3 icon and text Congratulations! On the left, new text appears: Tap 'View details'. Galaxy Watch8 screen is scrolled down and View details is tapped. Sequences shortened. Video simulated for illustrative purposes. Actual UI may be different. Running Coach program is available on Android phones (Android 10 or above) and requires Samsung Health app (v6.30.2 or above). Samsung account login required. To use Running Coach program, user needs to take a running level test and get a level before starting the coach program. Scene changes, text appears at the top: to see more details on the phone. Galaxy Watch8 and smartphone are in the middle, displaying details on the running test. Smartphone screen is scrolled down. Sequences shortened. Galaxy S25 Ultra sold separately. Video simulated for illustrative purposes. Actual UI may be different. Running Coach program is available on Android phones (Android 10 or above) and requires Samsung Health app (v6.30.2 or above). Samsung account login required. To use Running Coach program, user needs to take a running level test and get a level before starting the coach program. Scene changes, text appears in the middle: Planning to take your running to the next level? Above the text is a running icon that runs to the right. Scene changes. On the left is text Tap 'Running coach'. On the right is Galaxy Watch8 displaying Running coach notification with number 3 icon on the right and text 1. Low interval, 2.00 kilometers and 16 minutes at the bottom. The upper part of the notification is tapped and Running coach feature is onscreen. On the left, new text appears: Check out a workout plan tailored to you. The lower button on the side of Galaxy Watch8 is pressed and the screen displays the notification again. On the left, new text appears: Let's start your first workout. The bottom part of the notification displayed on Galaxy Watch8 is tapped. Text Workout 1, Low interval, 5 fire icons with 3 of them marked, text 2.00 kilometers, stats 07 minutes 00 seconds, 12 minutes 00 seconds, 16 minutes. On the left, new text appears: Review the details. Screen on Galaxy Watch8 is scrolled down and two buttons appear: Start and Settings. On the left, new text appears: Tap 'Start'. Start button displayed on Galaxy Watch8 is tapped. Screen changes and shows real-time workout stats including running time, Lap distance, Lap pace and heart rate. On the left, new text appears: Train at your own pace. New text appears: Your training is complete, nice work! Galaxy Watch8 displays checkmark icon, text Passed! and confetti in the background. On the left, new text appears: Check out daily insights from your training. Galaxy Watch8 displays running icon on the left and stats 2.50 kilometers, 20 minutes 52 seconds, 8 minutes 19 seconds per kilometer and 226 calories. Screen is scrolled down and View detail button appears. On the left, new text appears: Tap 'View detail'. View detail button displayed on Galaxy Watch8 is tapped. Sequences shortened. Video simulated for illustrative purposes. Actual UI may be different. Running Coach program is available on Android phones (Android 10 or above) and requires Samsung Health app (v6.30.2 or above). Samsung account login required. To use Running Coach program, user needs to take a running level test and get a level before starting the coach program. Scene changes. On the left is text See more details on your phone. On the right is a smartphone with details of the workout onscreen. Screen is scrolled down to show details. Galaxy S25 Ultra sold separately. Video simulated for illustrative purposes. Actual UI may be different. Running Coach program is available on Android phones (Android 10 or above) and requires Samsung Health app (v6.30.2 or above). Samsung account login required. To use Running Coach program, user needs to take a running level test and get a level before starting the coach program. Scene changes, text appears on the left: Completed over 70% of your sessions? On the right, Galaxy Watch8 displays the list of completed training sessions. On the left, new text appears: It's time to level up! Galaxy Watch8 screen is scrolled down and Level up test section is tapped. Level up test instructions appear onscreen. Screen is scrolled down and two buttons appear: Start and Settings. Start button is tapped. Real-time workout stats onscreen, displaying running time, Main distance, Main average and heart rate. On the left, new text appears: Run your way to the next level. New text appears: Congratulations, you did it! Keep on running. Galaxy Watch8 displays number 4 icon, text Level 4 and confetti in the background. Sequences shortened. Video simulated for illustrative purposes. Actual UI may be different. Running Coach program is available on Android phones (Android 10 or above) and requires Samsung Health app (v6.30.2 or above). Samsung account login required. To use Running Coach program, user needs to take a running level test and get a level before starting the coach program. Scene changes, text appears in the middle: From a beginner to a pro, run your best with Galaxy Watch. Scene changes. Galaxy Watch8 Classic is on its side and is slightly turned. Galaxy Watch8 appears in a slightly tilted front view and is placed next to Galaxy Watch8 Classic. Text Galaxy Watch8 Watch8 Classic. Scene changes. In the middle, samsung.com. Samsung logo. </span> </button> 
      </div> 
